INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Q1. Does a breakpoint terminate program execution?

Answer

No.

A breakpoint only pauses (suspends) program execution.
Execution can be resumed after inspection.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Does a breakpoint automatically detect bugs?

Answer

No.

A breakpoint only pauses execution.
The developer analyzes the application state to identify the bug.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Which breakpoint is most commonly used?

Answer

The Line Breakpoint is the most commonly used breakpoint during debugging.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Why use a Conditional Breakpoint instead of a normal breakpoint?

Answer

A normal breakpoint pauses every time the line is executed.

A conditional breakpoint pauses only when the specified condition evaluates to true, making debugging more efficient.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Can a Conditional Breakpoint improve debugging efficiency?

Answer

Yes.

It avoids unnecessary pauses and allows developers to inspect only the required execution scenario.

